														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2338013">
									

<p>Sorry for necro-posting; The problem is that tracking the homeless is difficult. If a hobo up and dies, and all anyone knows him as is &quot;Old Joe&quot;, then identifying him is difficult (which it mentions is possible, not just complete absence of identification).</p>
<p>Although I do have a problem with the DC area. Unless it's somehow drawing those qualified for the service to the area, there aren't THAT many DC vets unidentifiable. Or is it possible the fact point of origin is unknown, is because it can start anywhere, with D.C. being an endpoint? Lack of origin could be the old &quot;does nothing until un-observed&quot; trick.</p>

